(Bug #66, the sinks beyond a bare Print: a forward-declared global reaches a
 format hole, a property, arithmetic, an append and a copy into a local, and
 each one asked the same broken question - "what type is this name?" - of a
 table the walk had not filled yet. `Print "{label}"` printed the address
 inside the text; `names's first` printed the element's address; float
 arithmetic read the bits as an integer; appending to a forward buffer wrote
 through a slot typed as a number.)

To 'use them all'.
    Print "interp {label}".
    Print names's first.
    a float called doubled is ratio multiply 2.0.
    Print doubled.
    Append "DEF" to payload.
    Print payload.
    Append 4 to items.
    Print items.
    a text called copied is label.
    Print copied.
    Print anything.
    Print label's type.

a text called label is "hello".
a list called names is ["alpha", "beta"].
a float called ratio is 2.5.
a buffer called payload is "ABC".
a list called items is [1, 2, 3].
a value called anything is "vv".

'use them all'.
